Can't you just test for nomality?

object1 <- c(1, 1, 1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7, 7, 7, 7, 7,7,7, 8, 9, 9, 10)

# possibility 1
shapiro.test(object1)

	Shapiro-Wilk normality test
data:  object1
W = 0.8899, p-value = 0.03203

# possibility 2
ks.test(object1, "pnorm", mean=mean(object1), sd=sd(object1))

	One-sample Kolmogorov-Smirnov test
data:  object1
D = 0.2557, p-value = 0.1665
alternative hypothesis: two-sided

